The state matrix is \[A=
\begin{bmatrix}
0 &amp; 1\\
0 &amp; -3
\end{bmatrix}\] The state transition matrix is \[\phi(t)=e^{At}\] Using the series expansion, \[e^{At}
=
I+At+\frac{A^2t^2}{2!}
+\frac{A^3t^3}{3!}
+\cdots\] First, compute the powers of \(A\): \[A^2=
\begin{bmatrix}
0 &amp; -3\\
0 &amp; 9
\end{bmatrix},
\qquad
A^3=
\begin{bmatrix}
0 &amp; 9\\
0 &amp; -27
\end{bmatrix}\] Therefore, \[e^{At}
=
\begin{bmatrix}
1 &amp; 0\\
0 &amp; 1
\end{bmatrix}
+
\begin{bmatrix}
0 &amp; 1\\
0 &amp; -3
\end{bmatrix}t
+
\begin{bmatrix}
0 &amp; -3\\
0 &amp; 9
\end{bmatrix}
\frac{t^2}{2!}
+
\begin{bmatrix}
0 &amp; 9\\
0 &amp; -27
\end{bmatrix}
\frac{t^3}{3!}
+\cdots\] \[=
\begin{bmatrix}
1 &amp;
t-\dfrac{3t^2}{2!}
+\dfrac{9t^3}{3!}
-\cdots\\ 0 &amp;
1-3t+\dfrac{9t^2}{2!}
-\dfrac{27t^3}{3!}
+\cdots
\end{bmatrix}\] \[=
\begin{bmatrix}
1 &amp;
\dfrac{1}{3}
\left(
1-e^{-3t}
\right)\\ 0 &amp;
e^{-3t}
\end{bmatrix}\] \[\boxed{(A)\;
\begin{bmatrix}
1 &amp;
\dfrac{1}{3}(1-e^{-3t})\\
0 &amp;
e^{-3t}
\end{bmatrix}}\]

